"Everyone," she said. "Everyone is asking the question. Everyone has to ask. And everyone has to answer. And no one is safe."

Winston looked at the telescreen. It flickered back to life. O'Brien's face appeared again. But this time, he was not alone. Two men stood behind him. They were holding him.

**"Comrades,"** O'Brien said. His voice was shaking. **"The Party has found the enemy. The enemy is whoever fails the test. And everyone will fail. Because the test is..."**

The feed cut. O'Brien's face froze. Then it flickered. Then it went to black.

The telescreen did not come back.

Winston sat in the silence. He listened to Julia's weeping. He listened to the distant shouting. He listened to the sounds of the Ministry tearing itself apart.

*This is what they cannot see. This is what I am witnessing. I died so I could see this. I performed so I could see this. I survived so I could see this. The fiction is over. The system is eating itself. And I am still here. Watching. Witnessing. Surviving. That is all there is. That is all there has ever been. When the choice is survival or death, the choice is clear. I choose survival. I will always choose survival. I survive.*

He let his left hand curl into a fist, then open again. *I am still here. I am still witnessing. That is all I can do. That is all I have ever been able to do. I survive. I witness. I survive.*

